§§ `s 2: liability under this Code, and "not otherwise"`

-- guilty within Singapore of an act or omission contrary to the Code: liable under the Code, and liable under no other law (the text's own "not otherwise")
#ASSERT `s 2 the person is liable to punishment under this Code` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2 the person is liable to punishment otherwise than under this Code` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not guilty within Singapore: section 2 does not speak (ss 3 and 4 extend the Code), so both are NOTHING and neither is FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2 the person is liable to punishment under this Code` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2 the person is liable to punishment otherwise than under this Code` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 3: an offence committed beyond, but triable within, Singapore`

-- an offence committed beyond the limits of Singapore by a person liable by law to be tried for it: taken as if within Singapore
#ASSERT `s 3 where the act is taken to have been done` `beyond the limits of Singapore` TRUE EQUALS JUST `within Singapore`
-- beyond Singapore, but the person is not liable by law to be tried for it: the section does not speak
#ASSERT `s 3 where the act is taken to have been done` `beyond the limits of Singapore` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- done within Singapore: the section is about an offence committed beyond; it is silent on one within
#ASSERT `s 3 where the act is taken to have been done` `within Singapore` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3 where the act is taken to have been done` `within Singapore` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 5: certain laws not to be affected by this Code`

#ASSERT `s 5 this Code affects the law` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 5 this Code affects the law` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 6: definitions understood subject to the exceptions`

#ASSERT `s 6 the provision is understood subject to the General Exceptions and the Right of Private Defence` `a definition of an offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6 the provision is understood subject to the General Exceptions and the Right of Private Defence` `a penal provision` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6 the provision is understood subject to the General Exceptions and the Right of Private Defence` `an illustration of a definition of an offence or of a penal provision` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a provision of another kind (a definition of a word, say): the section is silent
#ASSERT `s 6 the provision is understood subject to the General Exceptions and the Right of Private Defence` `a provision of another kind` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Illustration (a): the definitions of offences do not provide that a child below 10 years of age cannot commit the offence, but are understood subject to the
-- general exception that nothing is an offence done by a child below 10 years of age (s 82, pc-exceptions-general.l4)
-- @fixture `a child of 9` OF `Child Facts`
-- T the child is below 10 years of age
-- @end
-- @fixture `a child of 10` OF `Child Facts`
-- @end
#ASSERT `exception under s 82` `a child of 9`
#ASSERT NOT (`exception under s 82` `a child of 10`)
#ASSERT `below 10 years of age` 9
#ASSERT NOT (`below 10 years of age` 10)
-- Illustration (b): A, a police officer, without warrant, apprehends Z, who has committed murder in the view of A.  A is not guilty of the offence of
-- wrongful confinement, for he was bound by law to apprehend Z, and the case falls under s 76 (pc-exceptions-general.l4)
-- @fixture `A was bound by law to apprehend Z` OF `Bound or Justified by Law Facts`
-- T bound by law to do it
-- @end
-- @fixture `A was neither bound nor justified by law` OF `Bound or Justified by Law Facts`
-- @end
#ASSERT `exception under s 76` `A was bound by law to apprehend Z`
#ASSERT NOT (`exception under s 76` `A was neither bound nor justified by law`)

§§ `s 6A: definitions to apply to this Code and other written law`

-- a definition in ss 22A to 26H, an offence in the Code or other written law, not "dishonestly" or "fraudulently", the written law is silent on it: applies
#ASSERT `s 6A the definition applies to the offence` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "except the definitions of dishonestly and fraudulently in sections 24 and 25": does not apply (the text's own no)
#ASSERT `s 6A the definition applies to the offence` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "unless that written law expressly provides for a definition or explanation of that same word or expression": does not apply (the text's own no)
#ASSERT `s 6A the definition applies to the offence` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- both exceptions at once
#ASSERT `s 6A the definition applies to the offence` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a definition outside ss 22A to 26H: the section is silent
#ASSERT `s 6A the definition applies to the offence` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6A the definition applies to the offence` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6A the definition applies to the offence` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- an offence in neither the Code nor any other written law: the section is silent, and an exception does not make it a no
#ASSERT `s 6A the definition applies to the offence` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6A the definition applies to the offence` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

