#ASSERT `s 32 the words extend to illegal omissions` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "except where a contrary intention appears from the context"
#ASSERT `s 32 the words extend to illegal omissions` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- words that do not refer to acts done: the section is silent, whatever the context
#ASSERT `s 32 the words extend to illegal omissions` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 32 the words extend to illegal omissions` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 33: "act" and "omission"`

#ASSERT `s 33(1) the word "act" denotes the doing` `a single act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 33(1) the word "act" denotes the doing` `a series of acts` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 33(1) the word "act" denotes the doing` `a single omission` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 33(1) the word "act" denotes the doing` `a series of omissions` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 33(1) the word "act" denotes the doing` `something that is neither an act nor an omission` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 33(1) the word "omission" denotes the doing` `a single omission` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 33(1) the word "omission" denotes the doing` `a series of omissions` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 33(1) the word "omission" denotes the doing` `a single act` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 33(1) the word "omission" denotes the doing` `a series of acts` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 33(1) the word "omission" denotes the doing` `something that is neither an act nor an omission` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 33(2) Illustration: A gives Z small doses of poison in Z's food at different times over a few days, intending to kill Z.  Z dies from poisoning, although it is not
-- known which of those doses (individually or collectively) caused Z's death.  "A has caused Z's death by poisoning."
#ASSERT `s 33(2) the person is regarded as having caused the effect by the series of acts` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the same where it is known which of the acts caused it: the answer to "which" changes nothing
#ASSERT `s 33(2) the person is regarded as having caused the effect by the series of acts` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no act in the series caused the effect, or it was not a series: the subsection is silent
#ASSERT `s 33(2) the person is regarded as having caused the effect by the series of acts` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 33(2) the person is regarded as having caused the effect by the series of acts` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 33(2) the person is regarded as having caused the effect by the series of acts` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 36: effect caused partly by act and partly by omission`

#ASSERT `s 36 causing the effect partly by an act and partly by an omission is the same offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 36 causing the effect partly by an act and partly by an omission is the same offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 36 causing the effect partly by an act and partly by an omission is the same offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 36 causing the effect partly by an act and partly by an omission is the same offence` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 36 Illustration: A intentionally causes Z's death, partly by illegally omitting to give Z food, and partly by beating Z.  "A has committed murder."
-- (s 32: "causes death by doing an act" is read as including an illegal omission)
-- @fixture `A intentionally causes Z's death partly by omitting to give food and partly by beating` OF `Homicide Facts`
-- E private defence = `no private defence`
-- S victim = "Z"
-- S the manner = "by illegally omitting to give the said Z food and by beating the said Z"
-- T causes death by doing an act
-- T with the intention of causing death
-- @end
-- @fixture `no private defence` OF `Private Defence Facts`
-- @end
#ASSERT `commits murder` `A intentionally causes Z's death partly by omitting to give food and partly by beating`
#ASSERT `s 36 causing the effect partly by an act and partly by an omission is the same offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 38: persons engaged in a criminal act may be guilty of different offences`

#ASSERT `s 38 the persons may be guilty of different offences` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 38 the persons may be guilty of different offences` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 38 Illustration: A attacks Z under such circumstances of grave provocation that his killing of Z would be only culpable homicide not amounting to murder.
-- B, having ill will towards Z and intending to kill him, and not having been subject to the provocation, assists A in killing Z.  Here, though A and B are both
-- engaged in causing Z's death, B is guilty of murder, but A is guilty only of culpable homicide.
-- (B's own state of mind is what the facts record: B intends Z's death and is not provoked)
-- @fixture `A, provoked, kills Z` OF `Homicide Facts`
-- E private defence = `no private defence`
-- S victim = "Z"
-- S the manner = "by attacking the said Z under grave provocation"
-- T causes death by doing an act
-- T with the intention of causing death
-- T whilst deprived of the power of self-control by grave and sudden provocation
-- T causes the death of the person who gave the provocation, or of any other person by mistake or accident
-- T the provocation is not sought or voluntarily provoked by the offender as an excuse for killing or doing harm to any person
-- T the offender did not know and had no reason to believe that the provocation was given by anything done in obedience to the law, or by a public servant in the lawful exercise of his powers
-- T the provocation is not given by anything done in the lawful exercise of the right of private defence
-- @end
-- @fixture `B, not provoked, assists A in killing Z` OF `Homicide Facts`
-- E private defence = `no private defence`
-- S victim = "Z"
-- S the manner = "by assisting A in killing the said Z"
-- T causes death by doing an act
-- T with the intention of causing death
-- @end
#ASSERT `commits culpable homicide not amounting to murder` `A, provoked, kills Z`
#ASSERT NOT (`commits murder` `A, provoked, kills Z`)
#ASSERT `commits murder` `B, not provoked, assists A in killing Z`
#ASSERT NOT (`commits culpable homicide not amounting to murder` `B, not provoked, assists A in killing Z`)

